r 2k games multiplayer  centric evolved to feel the pressure of  a rapidly declining player base not only  did the game received mixed reviews but  it's expensive DLC package certainly  didn't leave a good taste in any gamers  Mouse the game saw its player base  dwindle on almost a daily basis steadily  decreasing until turtle rocks to  had no choice but to swallow their pride  and to make the game free-to-play a last  resort for a game that released at full  retail making the game cost that nothing  effectively injected some life into the  title but the booze that didn't last  longer and he'll find yourself sitting  in a matchmaking Lobby for a long time  these days battleborn gearbox software  the studio behind the popular  borderlands series poured more than two  years worth of resources into the  creation of battleborn  only to have their first two-person game  completely overshadowed by blizzards  outstanding overwatch battleborn had  such a rough launch in fact that the  game only saw an abysmal 12000 101  concurrent players on release day and  absolutely plummeted in the days and  weeks that followed in a desperate  attempt to keep the game alive  the developers have made the game  essentially free to play sometimes a  stars just don't align Pokemon go my  antics mobile app Pokemon go it took the  world by storm when it launched in July  2016 by September however the game was  all but abandoned according to reports  Pokemon go peaked on July 13 2016 with a  twenty eight point five million users in  the United States alone nearly nine  million of those users quit playing by  the end of the month by the following  month almost two-thirds of the apps peak  users decided they'd had enough of the  craze nevertheless Niantic had a major  hit on their hands proving that the  Pokemon brand is as viable as ever Titan  4 released just a few months after the  Xbox one respawns first iteration in the  titanfall series was slated to be the  first true next-gen title sadly